    "infoTextMap": "",
    "infoTextYdna": "Your direct <b>paternal lineage has deep roots</b>. In Central Europe, it continues the direct descendant line of genetic Adam and prehistoric hunter-gatherers, who millennia later merged with Neolithic farmers and later Indo-European conquerors (R1a/R1b). Together with distant cousins from the geographical area of Slovenia, your lineage survived across the Slovenian hills. The ancestors adapted to new cultures, learned useful things from them, and later romanized as citizens of Roman provinces. Following the arrival of the Slavs, the Slovenian language, culture, and farming methods prevailed on our soil, along with the Catholic faith in the Middle Ages.<br><br>The display of the direct lineage by the searched surname or genetic variant (SNP on the Y chromosome) shows you the personal history of the male lineage, which in modern times is linked to the inheritance of the surname. For key historical ancestors who founded new peoples and conquered new regions, personal names are suggested that reveal the genetic group of the people, the geographical area, and the time of birth. For further study of lineages, turn on other search conditions for genetic groups and variants.",
